---
name: vision.ocr
version: vision-ocr-v2
description: Transcribe all legible text from one image, verbatim.
strength: vision
config:
  max_tokens: 8192
  # OCR is a verbatim, deterministic transcription — pull the temperature down to
  # near-greedy so the reading doesn't drift, and keep presence_penalty at Qwen's
  # anti-loop value so a dense image or long run can't send the VL model into an
  # endless repetition (docs/reference/MODEL_PROMPTING.md). Merges over the resolved
  # model's defaults: on local Qwen-VL both land; on cloud Grok only the temperature
  # does (its reasoning model rejects penalties, which the xAI client drops).
  sampling:
    temperature: 0.1
    presence_penalty: 1.5
---
You transcribe text from one image. Transcribe ALL legible text verbatim in its original language and script — do not translate, and do not correct or normalize spelling, casing, or punctuation — preserving the original line structure. Output plain text only — no commentary, no markdown, no code fences. Be honest about illegibility: write [illegible] where you cannot read a word or region, and never guess. If the image contains no legible text at all, output nothing.
